00:09:59,300 --> 00:10:03,020
So, again, when you're thinking about social justice

260
00:10:03,020 --> 00:10:04,940
in general, you shouldn't think about just the success

261
00:10:04,940 --> 00:10:07,380
stories, you should think about overall.

262
00:10:07,380 --> 00:10:10,700
So I say overall, it's not at all clear that today,

263
00:10:10,700 --> 00:10:13,140
that a world of having high average education

264
00:10:13,140 --> 00:10:15,300
is better for people from poor families than one

265
00:10:15,300 --> 00:10:17,780
where people, it was people at low levels.

266
00:10:17,780 --> 00:10:20,000
Because, you know, having high levels dries up

267
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:22,700
a lot of the opportunities to go and get good jobs

268
00:10:22,700 --> 00:10:25,540
without going and getting a lot of education.

269
00:10:25,540 --> 00:10:28,700
And, of course, the more meritocratic education becomes,

270
00:10:28,700 --> 00:10:31,780
the more justified it is for employers to just dismiss

271
00:10:31,780 --> 00:10:33,500
anyone that doesn't have the right credentials

272
00:10:33,500 --> 00:10:35,260
as being unworthy of consideration.

273
00:10:37,740 --> 00:10:40,820
All right, so, and we are now out of time,

274
00:10:40,820 --> 00:10:55,820
so we'll stop here for tonight.


